---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="General Ground Rules | Northumberland Sporting Clays"
  description="Our General Ground Rules"
>

<section>

  <header class="section-header">
    <h1>General Ground Rules</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="prose-container">

    <h2>Shooters</h2>
    <ol>
    <li>All persons must sign in before shooting</li>
    <li>Any person under 15 must be supervised by a shotgun certificate holder of, or over 21</li>
    <li>No alcohol is allowed on the ground before or during shooting</li>
    <li>No person who appears to be intoxicated or under the influence of drugs will be allowed on the shooting ground.</li>
    <li>The owners of any shotguns used on the ground are solely responsible for security of those guns as stated on their shotgun certificate.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Ammunition</h2>
    <ol>
    <li>Only fibre wads to be used.</li>
    <li>Only commercially loaded cartridges to be used (no home loads).</li>
    <li>No cartridge greater than 28 grams load and greater than English number 6 shot to be used.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Safety</h2>
    <ol>
    <li>All shooters must wear eye and ear protection</li>
    <li>Mounting of any gun for the purpose of checking ‘gun fit’ may only take place on a recognised shooting stand with the gun pointed in the normal shooting direction and empty, unless otherwise approved by the shoot manager.</li>
    <li>All spent cartridges to be placed in the approved bins.</li>
    <li>When on the shooting ground all guns must be carried to and from shooting stands in an unloaded condition AND in a gun slip or case.</li>
    <li>Under no circumstances will a person be allowed to have a loaded shotgun in his possession whether open or not, EXCEPT on a designated firing point.</li>
    <li>No shooting is allowed other than from a designated firing point.</li>
    <li>Shooting or attempted shooting of live quarry is not permitted at any time.</li>
    <li>No person should alter, attempt to alter or refill a trap unless they have been instructed in its safe and proper use.</li>
    <li>ANY person acting in a dangerous or irresponsible manner, whether shooting or not will be asked to leave the ground and reported to the CPSA or Police, whichever is deemed suitable. Bad language and abusive behaviour will also not be tolerated, please do not put us in the difficult position of having to ask you to leave.</li>
    <li>All shooting must cease immediately on hearing the safety whistle and guns unloaded. Shooting will only recommence on the authority of the shoot manager.</li>
    </ol>

  </div>

  </section>   

</BaseLayout>